WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.442 --> 00:00:01.650
(bright music)

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:02.970
- [Narrator] These photos show some

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:05.550
of Kim Jong Un's most
iconic public appearances

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:08.231
as North Korea's leader
over the past 12 years.

00:00:08.231 --> 00:00:10.140
(bright music)

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.060
From 2011, when he came to power

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:13.920
following his father's death,

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.480
to one of the many events he attended

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.960
as North Korea emerged from
the Coronavirus Pandemic.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.390
Jenny Town is the director of 38 North,

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:23.580
a North Korea focused website.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.520
She has been studying the
subtle shifts in Kim's attire

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:27.540
over the years.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.840
- Kim Jong Un is the face of North Korea

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:35.100
and the persona that he
puts out, really tells you

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.010
how he wants the people to see him.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.270
- [Narrator] We look
at what can be gleaned

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:41.190
about the changing state of North Korea

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:43.493
from Kim's wardrobe choices.

00:00:43.493 --> 00:00:44.730
(crowd cheers)

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:46.440
And what his different looks signal

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:47.990
about the future of his regime.

00:00:49.974 --> 00:00:52.890
(North Korean singing)

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:54.630
Kim Jong Un's public appearances

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.370
are all carefully choreographed

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:57.969
and often packed with symbolism.

00:00:57.969 --> 00:00:58.802
(horse hooves patter)

00:00:58.802 --> 00:01:01.800
In late 2019, Kim was pictured
riding on a white horse

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.300
through Mount Peaktu.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.670
The mountain is one of the
country's most sacred sites,

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:07.320
a place many North Koreans believe

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.170
to be where the first
Korean kingdom was founded.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.540
- These were special
horses that were gifted

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:14.010
to the Kim family.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.920
Only the leaders have
these special horses.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:18.840
They would only have a photo shoot here

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:22.050
if it was a very important
message they were trying to send.

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:24.000
This was, the North Koreans were going

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.470
to do it in their own way,

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:28.857
reasserting that self-reliance attitude.

00:01:28.857 --> 00:01:30.690
(crowd cheers and applauds)

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.190
- [Narrator] Descendants
of the Kim family,

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:35.340
namely Kim Jong Un's late
grandfather, Kim Il Sung,

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.170
and father, Kim Jong Il,

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:39.390
seen standing on the
mountain in this painting,

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.190
have run the country since its founding

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:42.990
more than 70 years ago.

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:45.840
In another painting of the two
former North Korean leaders

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:46.673
on the peak,

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:48.600
shows there's one outfit that's common

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.430
between all three Kims.

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:51.453
The Mao suit.

00:01:52.432 --> 00:01:53.550
(bright music)

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:56.250
The pointed collar, to the neck buttoning,

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:58.253
and the four pockets in the front.

00:01:58.253 --> 00:01:59.280
(crowd cheers)

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.290
The suit is known as
the Mao suit in the West

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:02.970
because they were
popularized during the reign

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:05.725
of Mao Zedong, the founder
of communist China.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:08.070
(military chanting)

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:10.740
It's one of Kim's most
common wardrobe choices.

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:13.380
- You can see here,
especially at the beginning

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.930
of Kim Jong Un's tenure as the leader,

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:18.755
you saw him wear this quite often.

00:02:18.755 --> 00:02:20.580
(brass band plays)

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.140
- [Narrator] Kim wore
the Mao suit when he met

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:25.200
with Chinese leader Xi Jinping,
during his first trip abroad

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.456
since coming to power, in 2018.

00:02:27.456 --> 00:02:28.289
(glasses clink)

00:02:28.289 --> 00:02:30.210
He also wore similar outfits in talks

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:31.770
with different world leaders

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:34.050
at a time when Pyongyang was negotiating

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:36.570
nuclear disarmament with the US.

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:37.500
- [Donald] My friend.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:38.940
- He met with Donald Trump.

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:42.270
He had this typical Mao suit on

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:46.500
that was very representative
of the North Korean identity.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:48.900
It might've been, yeah,
to differentiate himself

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:50.460
from the other world leaders

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.487
and to maintain that
North Korean presence.

00:02:53.487 --> 00:02:54.810
(bright music)
(crowd cheers)

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:57.330
- [Narrator] But Kim also
likes to wear Western suits,

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:59.640
especially while attending
events back home.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:02.820
Town says this shows Kim wants
to portray a different image

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.140
for the domestic audience.

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:06.360
- In one of his New Year's
speeches, he started

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:10.200
to wear these Western suits
in these formal meetings,

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.030
and especially the important ones.

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:14.970
There wasn't the Mao suit
anymore, domestically.

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:17.460
You saw much more of this global persona,

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:20.610
much more of this Western style look.

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:23.250
I think there was a
level of confidence here

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:27.570
and a trying to portray that
the country was moving forward

00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:31.263
and especially on equal terms
with the rest of the world.

00:03:32.236 --> 00:03:33.180
(bright music)

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:34.890
- [Narrator] Kim's
appearance before, during,

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:36.840
and after the COVID-19 pandemic

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.980
reflects his political messaging.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:40.200
(rocket ignites)

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.840
As negotiations over North
Korea's denuclearization

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.518
collapsed in 2019-

00:03:44.518 --> 00:03:46.020
(crowd cheers)

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:48.270
Kim made frequent public outings in a bid

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:49.740
to rally the country.

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:52.500
- He was out doing site
visits like this one here,

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:55.110
like he's, you know, out with the people

00:03:55.110 --> 00:04:00.110
in a pretty typical attire
that's seasonally appropriate,

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.250
but casual, to try and, you know,

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:04.470
connect with the people more.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:05.700
There was a lot of note

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.890
that he was out doing these site visits

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:10.254
maybe about every couple of weeks.

00:04:10.254 --> 00:04:12.180
(bright music)
(digital thermometer beeps)

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.350
- [Narrator] But when COVID-19 began

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:14.670
to spread across the globe

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:16.350
and North Korea closed its borders,

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:18.360
Kim barely appeared in public.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:22.560
- Towards the middle to end of
the pandemic we did see sort

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:24.630
of a new Kim Jong Un emerge.

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.280
You can see, especially in this picture,

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:28.560
how much thinner he is,

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:30.780
especially compared to this one here.

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:32.610
One of the narratives that went on at

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:36.660
that time domestically was
that the people were also

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:39.420
so concerned that he
had lost so much weight

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.010
and that he was suffering

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:43.740
for the people along with the people,

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:46.485
during a very difficult
time for the country.

00:04:46.485 --> 00:04:47.340
(ceremonial music)

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:49.080
- [Narrator] But as the
pandemic came to an end

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:51.420
and North Korea began
its gradual reopening,

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:53.910
Kim started to look
more like his old self.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:55.590
- There was definitely a shift

00:04:55.590 --> 00:05:00.590
in the public narrative in Kim
Jong Un's priorities as well.

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:04.711
A real shift towards more
military development.

00:05:04.711 --> 00:05:06.150
(missile launches)

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:08.460
We saw a lot of new missile systems

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:10.739
being tested and developed.

00:05:10.739 --> 00:05:11.970
(missile ignites)

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:14.490
We saw a lot more military activity

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:16.680
when the economy wasn't doing so good.

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:19.533
That does convey a sense of optimism.

00:05:20.742 --> 00:05:23.520
(upbeat music)

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:24.900
- [Narrator] In March, 2022,

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:27.630
North Korean state media
released a heavily edited video

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:29.430
showing Kim wearing sunglasses

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:32.040
and a black leather jacket
as he oversaw the test

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:34.470
of the new intercontinental
ballistic missile.

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:36.990
- For him to have come
out in this bomber jacket,

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:40.980
it really set the tone of trying
to create his own persona,

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:44.070
trying to look more Western.

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:47.997
Maybe it was trying to
look kind of like Top Gun,

00:05:47.997 --> 00:05:49.768
(soldier screams order)

00:05:49.768 --> 00:05:52.380
(missile ignites)

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:54.540
- [Narrator] The Top Gun style
jacket marked a shift away

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:56.640
from the outfits that symbolized the cult

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:59.490
of personality around his
father and grandfather.

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:02.280
- This is a good kind of
depiction of the evolution

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:04.530
of Kim Jong Un, and here we see him

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.870
with a much more traditional look,

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:09.330
trying to look like his grandfather,

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:13.740
trying to emulate that kind
of traditional persona.

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:14.910
And here he is.

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:16.230
He is his own man, right?

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:18.450
Like he's had a lot of successes,

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:21.780
especially in the military
front and the missile front,

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:23.070
and things that his father

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:25.992
and grandfather hadn't
been able to accomplish.

00:06:25.992 --> 00:06:27.000
(crowd cheers)

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.550
And we have seen Kim Jong
Un throughout this period

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:32.190
as he develops his own, not only style,

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:34.619
but also his own style of leadership.

00:06:34.619 --> 00:06:37.202
(upbeat music)

